{
  "_comment": [
    "Punch-list 3.6. The authority on what a hair groom IS, read by the build, by the asset gate",
    "Every groom below is one entry in hair_cards.py's HAIR_STYLES table — `--hair <id>` selects a",
    "SHAPE, not just an output directory. bob01 is the byte-identical control (sha256 98ca6c23...)",
    "that the style refactor was verified against and the original material measurements were taken",
    "on; it is DELIBERATELY not the corrected bob. bob02 is. See docs/research/hairstyle-targets.md.",
    "",
    "and by the runtime — the same arrangement assets/wardrobe/manifest.json has, and for the same",
    "reason: two files that each decide a garment's alphaMode independently will disagree, and the",
    "disagreement is invisible until a judge looks at a plate.",
    "",
    "Hair is deliberately NOT in the wardrobe manifest. It has no clo rating, no layer, no",
    "formality and cannot be taken off, so resolving it through the garment clause would make that",
    "clause the authority on a thing with none of the fields it reads.",
    "",
    "The GLBs beside this file are shipping Git LFS assets. Produce original exports with:",
    "  blender --background --python tools/figure-pipeline/build_figure.py --python-exit-code 1 -- \\",
    "      --gender 0.5 --output assets/figures/figure_g050.glb --hair bob01",
    "bob02/g050 additionally requires the calibrated hair_fall.mjs post-export step.",
    "See tools/figure-pipeline/README.md; direct regeneration without that step restores the cheek-wrap defect."
  ],
